research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-localization-bps.md:347:| V. Pestun, “Localization of Gauge Theory on a Four-Sphere and Supersymmetric Wilson Loops,” arXiv:0712.2824v3 (PDF title page 20 Sep 2012), `https://arxiv.org/pdf/0712.2824` | Retrieved PDF; inspected abstract/contents and §1 passages containing (1.3)–(1.5), the S4 assumptions around the instanton correction, and the explicit regulator caveat. Section headings and equation locations for §§2–5 were searched to orient later reading, but their determinant/localization proofs were not read in this pass. | Not full paper or appendices. In particular, the author explicitly does not construct the noncommutative S4 deformation and assumes it is well-defined and agrees with Nekrasov's R4 deformation near the poles. Treat the path-integral identity as formal/conditional, not a rigorous continuum theorem. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-localization-bps.md:348:| A. Kapustin, B. Willett and I. Yaakov, “Exact Results for Wilson Loops in Superconformal Chern–Simons Theories with Matter,” arXiv:0909.4559v4 (PDF dated 17 Dec 2010), `https://arxiv.org/pdf/0909.4559` | Retrieved PDF; inspected abstract/contents, setup and S3 localization passages in §§2–3, including saddle locus, gauge fixing, zero modes and the Cartan matrix integral. | Not the complete determinant appendices or all examples. The claimed scope is superconformal Chern–Simons–matter, with explicit U(N)/ABJM examples; do not extend automatically to every 3D `N=2` theory. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-localization-bps.md:349:| G. Festuccia and N. Seiberg, “Rigid Supersymmetric Theories in Curved Superspace,” arXiv:1105.0689v2 (PDF dated 17 May 2011), `https://arxiv.org/pdf/1105.0689` | Retrieved PDF; read the abstract, §1 and §2 general procedure including the auxiliary supergravity backgrounds and gravitino/Killing-spinor equations; inspected the stated S3×R/S3 qualifications. | Not a complete background classification. Their setup assumes the appropriate off-shell supergravity coupling and notes complex auxiliary/background values and reflection-positivity limitations. Each new background needs its own checked Killing-spinor solution. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-localization-bps.md:350:| N. Nekrasov, “Seiberg–Witten Prepotential from Instanton Counting,” hep-th/0206161 (18 Jun 2002), `https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0206161` | Retrieved PDF; read the introduction, §2.2 passages defining equivariant moduli-space integration, §§3.1–3.4 on ADHM, noncompactness/resolution and contour localization, and §4.2's equivariant K-theory/index view. Search hits in §3.5 locate the partition-indexed fixed-point discussion, but the tangent-weight derivation was not read in this pass. | Not a full audit of the gauge-theory path integral or every contour calculation. The paper itself identifies small-instanton and IR noncompactness, uses Ω/noncommutative regularization, and labels the KP/Toda relation conjectural. Instanton count is a formal/equivariant construction under its stated regulator, not a proof of a general continuum path integral. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-localization-bps.md-351-| D. Tong, “TASI Lectures on Solitons: Instantons, Monopoles, Vortices and Kinks,” arXiv:hep-th/0509216v5 (19 Dec 2005), `https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0509216` | Retrieved PDF; inspected §2.1–2.3 on SU(N) monopoles, charge sectors, Dirac quantization, the Bogomolny square completion and Prasad–Sommerfield example. | Pedagogical source, not an independent audit of all analytic existence/regularity theorems. The energy calculation is conditional on the specified classical action and asymptotics; the paper's 2005 observational statement is not carried forward as a current empirical-status claim. |
