research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md:317:## Equivariant localization: what the theorem proves
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-318-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-319-For a compact Lie group `K` acting smoothly on a manifold `X`, let `EK` be a
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-320-contractible free `K`-space and `BK=EK/K`. The Borel construction is
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-321-`EK x_K X=(EK x X)/K`, and its cohomology is the Borel equivariant cohomology
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-322-`H_K^*(X;R)`. The Cartan complex is
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-323-`(S(k^*) tensor Omega^*(X))^K` with total grading in which linear
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-324-coordinates on `k` have degree two. For polynomial `K`-equivariant forms
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-325-`alpha`, define `d_K alpha = d alpha - i_{X_xi} alpha`, where `xi` is the
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-326-formal Lie-algebra variable and `X_xi` the induced vector field. On invariant
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-327-forms, `d_K^2 alpha = -L_{X_xi}alpha = 0`; the final equality is exactly the
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md:328:invariance condition. This algebraic complex is not yet a localization
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-329-formula.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-330-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md:331:The finite-dimensional localization theorem requires its own exact
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-332-hypotheses: compact oriented `X`, a compact torus `T` action, an
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-333-equivariantly closed class, a coefficient field `k` equal to `Q` or `R`, and
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md:334:localization of `H_T^*(pt;k)` by the nonzero characters of `T`. Each fixed component must
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-335-be a smooth submanifold with an oriented normal bundle whose equivariant Euler
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-336-class is invertible in that localized ring; the integration map and degree
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-337-conventions are specified. Under those hypotheses the integral over `X`
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-338-equals the sum of fixed-component integrals divided by those Euler classes.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-339-The local proof obligation is the actual Borel/Atiyah–Bott or
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-340-Berline–Vergne argument, including orientation and denominator conventions;
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-341-the theorem is not supplied by the definition `d_K^2=0`.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md-342-
