research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/proposed-inventory.json-2811-      "candidate_contract": "| `thm-finite-dimensional-q-exact-deformation-invariance` | theorem | For the preceding data let `Q` be odd, `V` odd, `S` and the observable `O` even, require `Q^2V=0` (or that `Q^2` acts trivially on the integration cycle/integrand), `QS=QO=0`, and a `Q`-invariant measure and cycle (`div_μ Q=0` in coordinates). Prove `dZ_t/dt=0` by differentiating `∫O e^{-S-tQV}` and integrating the resulting `Q`-exact divergence. State a uniform integrable majorant for the derivative on every compact `t`-interval so differentiation/interchange is justified, and prove the boundary term vanishes (compact support or explicit decay). A large-`t` saddle limit additionally requires a proper coercive bosonic term, a characterized zero set, nondegenerate normal Hessian or a specified degenerate analysis, treatment of zero modes and a justified asymptotic limit. The finite-dimensional theorem does not establish a continuum Ward identity. |",
