+# Batch 47 authoring notes — Rigid Supersymmetric Backgrounds and Localization Data
+
+Run: \`advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23\`  
+Owned pair: \`qftx-susy-backgrounds\` / \`qftx-susy-backgrounds-examples\`  
+Scope: physics library, \`advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry\`, A-page order 1003.
+
+## Plan, inventory, and dependency levels
+
+The complete design at \`research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md\` § “Rigid Supersymmetric Backgrounds and Localization Data” (lines 653–660) agrees with the selected \`research/plan-spec.json\` entries: title, category, \`library: physics\`, A/B IDs, and \`requires: [qftx-susy-extended-actions, qftx-equivariant-cohomology]\` all match. There is no design/plan conflict. The proposed A inventory contains \`def-qftx-susy-background-data\` and \`post-qftx-rigid-supersymmetric-background\`; the initial B list is empty only as a planning placeholder. Under the current owner direction, two B examples were authored.
+
+The current page-level dependency graph records batch 47 at level 5, requiring batches 7 and 31. The item levels use the item-level rule from the dispatch, not those page levels:
+
+| Item | In-run item suppliers and current levels | Assigned item level |
+|---|---|---:|
+| \`def-qftx-susy-background-data\` | none | 0 |
+| \`post-qftx-rigid-supersymmetric-background\` | \`def-qftx-susy-background-data\` (0), planned \`post-qftx-n4-super-yang-mills-model\` (proposed contract has no item deps; provisional 0), \`def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model\` (2) | 3 |
+| \`ex-qftx-susy-flat-torus-geometric-background\` | \`def-qftx-susy-background-data\` (0) | 1 |
+| \`ex-qftx-susy-round-s4-localization-data\` | definition (0), postulate (3), planned N=4 model (provisional 0), Cartan definition (2) | 4 |
+
+No item cycle was found. The batch level remains 5 because the A page requires batch 31 at level 4. The item-level assumptions involving the absent N=4 model remain provisional and must be recomputed against its actual carrier when it arrives.
+
+## Current supplier inspections and disposition
+
+- \`qftx-equivariant-cohomology\` is present at \`library/quantum-field-theory-mathematics/qftx-equivariant-cohomology.md\`. Its exact definition \`def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model\` was read in full. Its source interface defines Borel and real Cartan equivariant cohomology for a compact torus and proves \(d_T^2=0\) on invariant forms; it expressly makes no general Borel–Cartan isomorphism claim. \`loadStep1Record\` plus \`step1Decision\` reports current \`ready\`, hash \`5487bc1bcee36dafba1b3e4747874ed8427cefc586a5a1f8ec92687e20924551\`. Draft status and pending later acceptance are not prerequisites.
+- \`qftx-susy-extended-actions\` is listed in batch 31, whose current A/B manifest has empty item arrays; its local library page and the planned \`post-qftx-n4-super-yang-mills-model\` carrier are absent. The exact available N=4 candidate interface in \`proposed-inventory.json\` is one vector plus three adjoint chiral multiplets, equivalent component content, and fixed trace/coupling convention. \`loadStep1Record\` plus \`step1Decision\` returns “Readiness record missing”; the carrier itself is absent. This is a real unresolved consuming input, not a draft/pending-review issue. The postulate and S4 example are fully authored conditionally on that exact planned interface and are marked escalated below. No batch-31 supplier was authored.
+- Batch 31’s design at track lines 429–438 and its assigned \`beta-31.task.md\` were read as context. Its page requires the N=1 superspace/action and non-Abelian Yang–Mills pages; the batch 47 notes do not infer their proof status or add unsupported rows for them.
+- No established prerequisite is newly classified as an open problem. The missing local N=4 postulate is an authoring/readiness obligation for its owner.
+
+## Item checkpoints
+
+### \`def-qftx-susy-background-data\`
+
+Claim: defines Euclidean four-dimensional spin/R background data, model-specific Killing-spinor equations, off-shell multiplets and \(Q^2\), and the full gauge-fixing/contour/measure/regulator input needed before a localization claim. It explicitly treats spin structure and connection as supplied data and does not claim that arbitrary metrics admit a solution or that a formal \([D\Phi]\) is a constructed measure.
+
+Conventions: natural units \(c=\hbar=1\); Euclidean signature; oriented Riemannian four-manifold; \(SO(4)\)/\(\operatorname{Spin}(4)\) quaternion convention; smooth principal-bundle right-action convention; countable-choice base inherited from the imported frame-bundle definition. The statement is uninterrupted; links are in its immediate Definition references section.
+
+Dependencies: the pinned mathematical definitions of smooth/Riemannian manifolds, frame and oriented-frame bundles, principal bundles/connections, associated vector bundles, and the Levi-Civita connection. No in-run logical suppliers. Item level 0.
+
+Sources read: Festuccia–Seiberg, arXiv:1105.0689, §2 equations (2.9)–(2.11), and §4 equation (4.1); Pestun, arXiv:0712.2824, §2 equations (2.5)–(2.14), (2.26)–(2.30), and §4.1–§4.3; Peelaers full lecture notes, §1.1–§1.2. Festuccia–Seiberg is used for the general rigid-limit distinction only; its old-minimal N=1 S4 reality statement is not transferred to the N=4 model. Pestun/Peelaers support the N=2/S4 background conventions and conditionality. Mechanical source fetch stamp and final scoped validation are pending.
+
+### \`post-qftx-rigid-supersymmetric-background\`
+
+Claim: adopts a particular massless N=4 \(SU(2)\) model on the round \(S^4_r\), explicit conformal Killing spinors, seven-auxiliary one-generator off-shell closure, R/gauge/isometry \(Q^2\), Faddeev–Popov gauge fixing, zero-mode/contour convention, and the assumed noncommutative \(\Omega\)-regulator extension. It states no constructed continuum measure or localization theorem.
+
+Conventions: Pestun’s \((9,1)\) dimensional-reduction notation with Euclidean four-sphere, \(\Phi_0=i\Phi_0^E\), \(K_i=iK_i^E\), \(a_0=ia_0^E\), source gamma matrices, \(r\) of length, \(g_{\rm YM}\) dimensionless, and \(\varepsilon_1=\varepsilon_2=r^{-1}\). The \(SU(2)\) trace normalization is explicit and remains conditional on the absent N=4 model interface.
+
+Dependencies: \`def-qftx-susy-background-data\), \`def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model\), and missing planned supplier \`post-qftx-n4-super-yang-mills-model\). The latter’s current authoring readiness was checked with both required helpers; carrier and readiness row are missing. Readiness is escalated until the actual supplier interface exists and is inspected. No proof or acceptance is attributed to its plan label.
+
+Sources read: Pestun, §1 equations (1.3)–(1.4) plus the explicit caveat that the S4 noncommutative deformation is assumed, not constructed; §2 equations (2.1)–(2.14), (2.26)–(2.30); §4.1–§4.3 equations (4.1)–(4.15); Appendix C equations (C.1)–(C.17), including the auxiliary-field off-shell closure reasoning. Peelaers §1.1–§1.2 supplies an independent lecture treatment and explicitly lists measure/off-shell hypotheses. Festuccia–Seiberg §2 is context for frozen supergravity backgrounds, not the N=4 S4 source. The full-text source-fetch stamp and final scoped checks are pending.
+
+### \`ex-qftx-susy-flat-torus-geometric-background\`
+
+Claim: exhibits a nonzero parallel spinor on the explicitly trivial periodic spin bundle over a flat four-torus and explains why this geometric input alone is not a localization package. This is a local conditional calculation, not a field-theory or measure claim.
+
+Dependencies: \`def-qftx-susy-background-data\), level 1. Proof steps 1.1–1.2 are complete; formatting/contract checks are pending. Festuccia–Seiberg §2 is context-only; the existence of the constant section is proved in-item.
+
+### \`ex-qftx-susy-round-s4-localization-data\`
+
+Claim: checks the source-postulated combined \(Q=s+\delta\) square and separates the finite smooth circle action on \(S^4\) from any infinite-dimensional field-space assertion. It leaves the measure, regulator extension, and \(t\to\infty\) limit at their actual formal status.
+
+Dependencies: \`def-qftx-susy-background-data\), \`post-qftx-rigid-supersymmetric-background\), \`post-qftx-n4-super-yang-mills-model\), and \`def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model\). Item level 4. Readiness is escalated because the N=4 model carrier is absent. Its verification contract is conditional on the adopted postulate and explicitly does not prove a continuum result.
+
+## Source retrieval and next actions
+
+Full PDFs were retrieved to task-specific files under \`/tmp\` and inspected with MuPDF text extraction; source-fetch-check stamps have not yet been run. No retrieval failed, so there is no dropped-source or alternative-proof resolution record. The coverage file will record per-item dispositions and limitations, then \`source-fetch-check --stamp\` will record actual fetch attempts and hashes. Next: generate the full item manifest, coverage, proof contracts and cross-batch dependency array; run source-fetch-check and required scoped checks; record the two genuinely blocked readiness rows as escalated and the two complete local rows as ready.
+
