+
+5.1 The element $a_0$ is a constant gauge parameter and $\omega$ generates the selected smooth circle isometry of $S^4_r$. Thus the square is a gauge transformation plus an isometry on the fields. The induced circle action on $S^4_r$ satisfies the compact-group and smooth-action hypotheses in [F2], so its ordinary geometric Cartan complex is defined. This use is only on $S^4_r$ and does not transfer the finite-dimensional definition to the field configuration space. [A1, A2, A3, F1, F2, step 2.1, step 3.1, step 4.1]
+
+6.1 The adopted contour, measure, and S4 regulator extension are explicit formal inputs in [A4]; the verification above neither constructs them nor proves a regulator-removal or $t\to\infty$ limit. [A4, step 5.1] ∎
